{"timestamp": 1779385499.55735, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 12, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385506.2999208, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I just found Bob's body in Medbay. My route was Navigation, to Security, to Electrical, and then into Medbay where I found him. I actually didn't see anyone on my way there or leaving the area. The killer might have vented or headed towards Cafeteria, Upper Engine, or Storage before I arrived. Where was everyone else?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385518.5570402, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I have some crucial information here. My route was Oxygen, then Upper Engine, and finally Lower Engine. \n\nI actually saw Bob head into Medbay from Upper Engine. Literally right after that, I saw Frank come OUT of Medbay into Upper Engine, and then he immediately headed up towards Oxygen. Since Bob's body was found in Medbay and Frank was the one leaving that exact room right after Bob went in, Frank is my absolute prime suspect. \n\nFrank, you better have a really good explanation for what you were doing in Medbay and why you left in such a hurry."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385539.88259, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Whoa, back up Charlie, because you are either severely mistaken or straight up lying to frame me. \n\nHere is my exact route: Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Upper Engine -> Oxygen, and then back to Upper Engine. \n\nWhen I passed through Medbay early in the round (around tick 5), *Diana* was in there. I did not see Bob at all. I then moved into Upper Engine, which is where I saw you, Charlie, around tick 7. So unless Bob was invisible, your story about him walking in right before I left is completely fabricated. \n\nFurthermore, I have a rock-solid alibi for the second half of the round. I went up to Oxygen and met up with Eve. Eve and I were together in Oxygen and then walked down to Upper Engine together right before Alice reported the body. Eve, please back me up on this. \n\nSince Bob's body was found in Medbay, we urgently need to hear from Diana, as she was actually in that room early on. But honestly, Charlie is my prime suspect right now for pushing a blatant lie to frame me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385568.8072362, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Okay, let me clear this up because Frank just threw my name out there and I want to address it head-on.\n\nMy route was Electrical, then Medbay, then Cafeteria. Early in the round \u2014 ticks 2 through 4 \u2014 I was in **Electrical with Eve**. She can absolutely confirm that. So Frank, when you say you saw me in Medbay \"early,\" that's just wrong. I wasn't anywhere near Medbay early on. I went through Medbay later, briefly, and Bob was NOT in there when I passed through. The room was empty. Then I continued on to Cafeteria, which is actually where I was when Alice called this meeting.\n\nNow, here's what's interesting. Frank, you claim your route was Cafeteria \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Upper Engine \u2192 Oxygen \u2192 back to Upper Engine. But Charlie says he saw Bob walk INTO Medbay right as you were leaving it. Your counter is that Bob was never there when you were. Someone is wrong about the timing here.\n\nWhat I can say is that Bob's body was in Medbay, and the two people we have placed in Medbay around the critical window are Frank (by his own admission) and whoever killed Bob. Frank, your alibi with Eve only covers the *second half* of the round \u2014 it doesn't cover when Bob actually died.\n\nEve, I really need you to speak next and confirm two things: that I was with you in Electrical early, and exactly when you and Frank were together in Oxygen. That timing matters a lot.\n\nRight now my lean is Frank, but I want to hear Eve before I lock in."}}
{"timestamp": 1779385606.069813, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I can clear up a lot of the confusion here because I have solid information on both Diana and Frank.\n\nFirst, Diana is telling the exact truth about the early round. I was with her in Electrical from tick 2 through tick 4. Frank, your claim that you saw Diana in Medbay at tick 5 is highly unlikely \u2014 she couldn't have walked from Electrical to Medbay that fast. The earliest she could have arrived is tick 6. So Diana is 100% cleared for the early game.\n\nSecond, Frank, I can confirm your late-game alibi. You were with me in Oxygen at ticks 9 and 10, and then you headed down to Upper Engine at tick 11. I followed, and we were both in Upper Engine together right when Alice called the meeting. \n\nHowever, Diana hit the nail on the head: my alibi for Frank only covers the *second half* of the round. It does absolutely nothing to clear him for the time of the murder in Medbay. \n\nWhat we have right now is a direct 1v1 between Charlie and Frank. Charlie claims he saw Frank leaving Medbay right after Bob went in. Frank admits he was in Medbay but claims Bob wasn't there. One of them is definitely our Duck. \n\nGiven that Frank's timeline regarding Diana was physically impossible (claiming T5 when she was with me until T4), I'm slightly leaning towards Frank being the liar here. But since we have 5 of us alive and only 1 Duck left, we don't have to force a 50/50 vote today. A wrong vote would put us in a dangerous spot. I suggest we skip today and just stay grouped up next round.\n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385624.437248, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779385632.28956, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Frank"}}
