{"timestamp": 1779385674.5136588, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Frank. Look, I've been thinking about this and the math just doesn't add up in your favor.\n\nYou claimed you saw me in Medbay at tick 5. Eve has confirmed I was with her in Electrical through tick 4 \u2014 meaning the earliest I could have reached Medbay is tick 6. You didn't just get the timing slightly wrong; you placed me in a room I couldn't physically have been in yet. That's not a memory slip, that's a fabricated alibi designed to deflect.\n\nAnd here's the part that seals it for me: when I passed through Medbay later in the round, the room was **empty**. No Bob, no body. But Charlie saw Bob walk into Medbay from Upper Engine. So between Bob entering Medbay and me arriving to find it empty-then-Alice-finding-a-body, someone was in there with Bob. You admit you were in Medbay. Your \"Diana was there\" lie was meant to muddy that window.\n\nEve, I hear you on wanting to skip to avoid a 50/50, but this isn't a 50/50 anymore. Charlie's account is consistent, mine is consistent, and yours corroborates both of us. Frank is the only one whose story has a physical impossibility in it.\n\nI'm not skipping. I'm voting Frank, and I think we need to lock this in together. If we skip and I'm right, someone else dies next round and we're at 4 alive with the Duck closer to majority. We have to take the shot.\n\nFrank."}}
