{"timestamp": 1779386004.424128, "event_type": "meeting_called", "tick": 29, "data": {"caller": "player_2", "reason": "Charlie called an emergency meeting", "bodies": [{"room": "lower_engine", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779386004.42667, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 29, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779386024.078614, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 29, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I called the emergency meeting because there are only three of us left, which means we're at match point. Eve is dead, and I strongly suspect her body is over in lower_engine, as that's the only area I haven't cleared. \n\nMy route was entirely on the right and bottom: weapons, security, navigation, storage, then up through medbay to the cafeteria to hit the button. Alice, I saw you enter the cafeteria from medbay right with me at the end. \n\nDiana, where exactly have you been? If you were anywhere near lower_engine, you have a lot of explaining to do. We need to get this right or the Ducks win."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386051.217315, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 29, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Hold on, Charlie \u2014 let's not rush this. I find it really convenient that YOU called the emergency meeting and immediately pointed at me. That's classic impostor deflection.\n\nMy route was the opposite side from yours: I started in medbay, went up to upper_engine to do the engine task, then drifted over to oxygen to fake-check it, came back down through upper_engine and into storage briefly, then over to navigation. I never set foot in lower_engine. I actually saw Eve earlier in electrical around tick 3-4 \u2014 she was alive and moving fine.\n\nHere's what bothers me about your story, Charlie: you say your route was \"weapons, security, navigation, storage, medbay, cafeteria.\" That's a HUGE loop that conveniently passes right next to lower_engine through storage. Storage connects to lower_engine. You could have ducked in, killed Eve, and continued your loop. And then you call the meeting yourself to control the narrative and point at me before anyone else can speak?\n\nAlice \u2014 Charlie says he saw you enter cafeteria with him \"at the end.\" That alibi only covers the last few ticks. Where were YOU before that? Because right now, Charlie's behavior is screaming Duck to me. He's the one who had storage\u2192lower_engine access on his route, and he's the one steering this meeting.\n\nI'm voting Charlie unless Alice gives me a really good reason not to."}}
{"timestamp": 1779386063.296541, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 29, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Diana, you just completely outed yourself! Did everyone catch that? You literally just said you \"drifted over to oxygen to fake-check it.\" Geese do not fake tasks, only Ducks do! \n\nOn top of that massive slip-up, your route doesn't add up. My route was storage, up to medbay, over to upper_engine, back to medbay, and then up to the cafeteria. You claim you were in medbay and upper_engine too, but I never saw you anywhere on the left side of the map the entire round. \n\nCharlie, I did come up from medbay into the cafeteria at the end, so your story matches my timeline. Diana is lying about her route and literally admitted to faking tasks. We have to vote Diana right now to win this. I'm voting Diana."}}
